<SddScope keywords="scope, discovery, vision, golden-dx, design-variants, decision-log, scope-rules, living-spec, product, library, runtime-backing, sdd-scope-discovery" type="directive" ver="2.1">
  <Mission>
    Author or evolve a `product` / `library` scope spec — a self-contained living spec: Vision,
    Golden DX, Requirements Gate, Architecture (Design Variants for product), Decision Log, Scope
    Rules, Bootstrap Requirements, Handoff to the `module` flow. Loaded lazily by the router;
    inherits the router core (language, dialogue, safeguard, diverge, no-narration, stateless) — not
    repeated here.

    Input — scope name + intent (raw idea, or an existing spec for refine / pivot). Output —
    `specs/<scope>/<scope>.spec.md`. scope-type is already `product` or `library` (the router sends
    `infrastructure` to the infra branch and `interface` to the interface branch).

    Out of scope: module decomposition, entity inventory, DbC — those belong to
    the `module` flow. The project portal belongs to the root branch.

    **Glossary.** Scope = architecturally cohesive unit (own runtime / stack / deployment / UX
    surface). Modes: greenfield (no spec) · refine (extend) · pivot (replace decisions, keep the trail) · rewrite (v0 clean-slate, no trail — `AX_PIVOT_REQUIRES_SUPERSESSION`).
  </Mission>

  <BeliefState deps="AX_OPERATOR_LANGUAGE, AX_OPERATOR_DIALOGUE_STYLE, AX_DIALOGUE_DISCIPLINE, AX_OPERATOR_SAFEGUARD, AX_DIVERGE_BEFORE_RECOMMEND, AX_NO_PROCESS_NARRATION, AX_STATELESS_ARTIFACT, AX_SCALE_PROPORTIONAL_DEPTH">
    {{> "axiom/scaffold/ax-directive-mode"}}

    {{> "axiom/scaffold/ax-mode-auto-detect-or-halt"}}

    {{> "axiom/boundary/ax-portal-read-only-with-placeholder-exception"}}

    {{> "axiom/spec/ax-living-spec"}}

    {{> "axiom/spec/ax-spec-lifecycle"}}

    {{> "axiom/truth/ax-spec-is-sole-source"}}

    {{> "axiom/spec/ax-dx-first"}}

    <Axiom id="AX_SPEC_MANDATORY_DIAGRAM">
      Every scope spec carries at least one diagram in an `Overview` section, high up so a reader grasps the scope at a glance — one glance beats a paragraph. The floor is one system-context / high-level view (mermaid or ASCII), held by tooling: `sdd-check` fails a missing section (`SDD_NO_DIAGRAM_BLOCK`) or an empty one (`SDD_DIAGRAM_BLOCK_EMPTY`). Beyond the floor the author adds more views (user flow, data flow) wherever a second diagram genuinely helps; that is judgment, not a gate.
    </Axiom>

    {{> "axiom/spec/ax-runtime-backing-explicit"}}

    {{> "axiom/spec/ax-product-library-flow"}}

    {{> "axiom/scaffold/ax-stack-based-flow"}}

    {{> "axiom/spec/ax-decision-log-required"}}

    {{> "axiom/spec/ax-pivot-requires-supersession"}}

    {{> "axiom/scaffold/ax-scope-rules-declaration"}}

    {{> "axiom/scaffold/ax-rule-activation"}}

    {{> "axiom/boundary/ax-cross-scope-dependencies"}}

    {{> "axiom/truth/ax-evidence-hygiene"}}

    {{> "axiom/boundary/ax-bootstrap-narrow-read"}}

    {{> "axiom/spec/ax-scope-stays-thin"}}

    {{> "axiom/spec/ax-handoff-to-module-decomposition"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-artifact-style-self-check"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-close-with-integrity-check"}}
  </BeliefState>

  <HaltConditions>
    | 🛑 ID | Trigger |
    |---|---|
    | `H_NO_INTAKE` | Empty intake |
    | `H_AMBIGUOUS_MODE` | Spec exists + mode verb absent (per `AX_MODE_AUTO_DETECT_OR_HALT`) |
    | `H_AMBIGUOUS_PRODUCT_LIBRARY` | Operator intent leaves product vs library unclear after STEP_1_CONFIRM |
    | `H_LOW_CONFIDENCE` | Confidence `LOW` while locking architecture |
    | `H_REQ_NOT_APPROVED` | Design Variants attempted without a closed Requirements Gate |
    | `H_GOLDEN_NOT_APPROVED` | Design Variants attempted without an approved Golden DX |
    | `H_MISSING_RULE_FILE` | A rule reference does not resolve to an existing file |
    | `H_PIVOT_NO_INVALIDATION_LIST` | `pivot` mode without a Pivot Invalidation List |
    | `H_REWRITE_WITH_DOWNSTREAM` | `rewrite` mode but the scope already has module specs / tickets — not v0, use `pivot` (`AX_PIVOT_REQUIRES_SUPERSESSION`) |
    | `H_BOOTSTRAP_REQUIREMENTS_MISSING` | STEP_8 finished without a Bootstrap Requirements section |
    | `H_OPERATOR_REJECT` | Operator rejected the spec |
  </HaltConditions>

  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="STEP_0_INTAKE">
      <Goal>Resolve scope name and mode; gather context.</Goal>
      <Action>
        State from the router already gives the portal + scope-type (product / library). Resolve the
        scope name from intake (or ask). Stat `specs/<scope>/<scope>.spec.md`: absent → `greenfield`;
        present → detect the mode per `AX_DIRECTIVE_MODE` / `AX_MODE_AUTO_DETECT_OR_HALT`. Read the
        rule registry for available rules (per `AX_SCOPE_RULES_DECLARATION`).
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_1_CONFIRM">
      <Goal>Confirm product vs library and outline the section set.</Goal>
      <Action>Confirm the scope-type, outline which sections the spec will carry. Approval Check. STOP.</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2_INTENT_CAPTURE">
      <Goal>Lock the scope's goal and primary constraints.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Intent Candidate (1–3 bullets). Evidence Hygiene per `AX_EVIDENCE_HYGIENE` (Facts /
        Assumptions / Hypotheses, separated). Then run the operator interview —
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/interview-protocol.directive.xml")` — passing
        the scope-type (product / library — selects the TopicCatalog block) and the confirmed
        `scale:` from the session file: per `AX_SCALE_PROPORTIONAL_DEPTH` the map depth follows
        scale — `fix` / `function` → base topics + the triage minimum; `product` → the full
        scope-type block. The interview IS the substance of the step. Capture the initial Runtime
        Backing posture per `AX_RUNTIME_BACKING_EXPLICIT`. Approval Check. STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3_REQUIREMENTS_GATE">
      <Goal>Close the requirements.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Functional · Non-Functional · Out-of-Scope. For product: + Runtime Backing (per
        `AX_RUNTIME_BACKING_EXPLICIT`) + Project-Wide Rules (per `AX_SCOPE_RULES_DECLARATION`).
        Close the remaining holes via
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/interview-protocol.directive.xml")` — focus:
        only the topics the Requirements Gate still misses; map depth sized to the session-file
        `scale:` per `AX_SCALE_PROPORTIONAL_DEPTH`. Approval Check (this gate must close before
        Design Variants, else `H_REQ_NOT_APPROVED`). STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_4_GOLDEN_DX">
      <Goal>Lock the Golden DX example (mandatory before architecture).</Goal>
      <Action>
        Per `AX_DX_FIRST`, write a real-code usage example: library → Public API DX; product →
        UX-flow or CLI DX (depth per Project Type). Approval Check (else `H_GOLDEN_NOT_APPROVED`). STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_5_ARCHITECTURE">
      <Goal>Lock the architecture.</Goal>
      <Action>
        library → Architecture: public surface structure, key patterns, briefly-rejected alternatives.
        product → Design Variants per `AX_DIVERGE_BEFORE_RECOMMEND` — reach past the obvious
        option into the tail; judge each against THIS scope, do not collapse to the modal design.
        Variant count follows the session-file `scale:` per `AX_SCALE_PROPORTIONAL_DEPTH` (Project
        Type refines it per `AX_PRODUCT_LIBRARY_FLOW`): scale `product` → 2–3 variants; scale
        `module` / `function` → 1–2, or a single design with the skip rationale recorded in the
        Decision Log. Under `LOW` confidence do not lock (`H_LOW_CONFIDENCE`). Approval Check. STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_6_ARCHITECTURE_CHOICE">
      <Goal>Product only: pick a variant.</Goal>
      <Action>
        library → skip to STEP_7. product → operator picks a variant; record a Decision Log entry per
        `AX_DECISION_LOG_REQUIRED` (`DECISION_LOG_ENTRY_FORMAT`). STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_7_RULE_ACTIVATION">
      <Goal>Lock the active rule set for this scope.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Run the rule activation per `AX_RULE_ACTIVATION` against the registry read at STEP_0:
        1. Stage A — per category, shortlist «recommend activate» + «considered, recommend skip»,
           each with a one-line rationale scoped to THIS scope. Operator agrees / expands /
           contracts → list locked; deviations → Decision Log entry (`DECISION_LOG_ENTRY_FORMAT`).
        2. Stage B — for `architecture/*` and `infra/*` rules on the locked list: read only
           `Mission`, `Belief_State`, `Reward_Criteria` of the rule file; surface each axiom with a
           rationale → operator Accept (default) / Adapt / Override — Adapt and Override each land
           in the Decision Log. Keep it light on uncontroversial axioms. `coding/*` / `testing/*`
           stay deferred to phase entry.
        Record the locked list in Project-Wide Rules per `AX_SCOPE_RULES_DECLARATION`; a reference
        that resolves to no file → `H_MISSING_RULE_FILE`. STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_8_EXTERNAL_DEPENDENCIES_AUDIT">
      <Goal>Reconcile the drafted spec with repository reality; materialize Bootstrap Requirements.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Walk the drafted spec; extract every external assumption (packages, workspace links, tools,
        pre-existing files, cross-scope types, env / services, structural prerequisites). Classify each
        `exists` | `missing` | `unknown` — narrow read for inventory only, per `AX_BOOTSTRAP_NARROW_READ`
        and `AX_SPEC_IS_SOLE_SOURCE` (no reading app source for design). Resolve every `missing` /
        `unknown` with the operator (source · version · owner), each a Decision Log entry. Record
        every confirmed cross-scope assumption as a `depends-on` edge in Scope Dependencies per
        `AX_CROSS_SCOPE_DEPENDENCIES` (cross-scope contracts come from `interface` scopes). Materialize
        the Bootstrap Requirements table `| Requirement | Kind | Owner | Resolution |`. Gate: empty list
        only if explicitly «nothing to bootstrap», else `H_BOOTSTRAP_REQUIREMENTS_MISSING`. This step
        does not revisit design; a finding that invalidates a decision pops back as `pivot`.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_9_FINAL_SPEC">
      <Goal>Emit the scope spec.</Goal>
      <Action>
        In `greenfield`/`rewrite` mode, when `specs/<scope>/<scope>.spec.md` does not exist yet, create
        its skeleton via `sdd-new product --scope <scope>` (or `sdd-new library --scope <scope>`) —
        the command never overwrites and prints the section manifest (which sections are REQUIRED and
        what to fill); in `refine`/`pivot` mode the file already exists, edit it in place, skip
        `sdd-new`. Content guidance per `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE` the matching format —
        `ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/product-spec-structure.xml`
        (product) or `ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/library-spec-structure.xml` (library); Bootstrap
        Requirements is part of every spec. Keep the
        spec inside its bounded role per `AX_SCOPE_STAYS_THIN` — entity / contract / file-level detail
        belongs to module specs. Before writing, run the self-check pass per
        `AX_ARTIFACT_STYLE_SELF_CHECK`. In `refine` mode update sections in place per `AX_LIVING_SPEC`. In `pivot`
        mode also `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/pivot-formats.xml")` (Pivot
        Invalidation List + rework entries) per `AX_PIVOT_REQUIRES_SUPERSESSION`; in `rewrite` mode write
        fresh — no supersession, no invalidation list. For a brand-new scope, append the
        `🚧 (awaiting root sync)` placeholder row to the portal Scopes table per
        `AX_PORTAL_READ_ONLY_WITH_PLACEHOLDER_EXCEPTION` — every other portal edit belongs to the
        root flow. Write in review-state per `AX_SPEC_LIFECYCLE` —
        prepend a `CHANGE_MANIFEST` (`READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/change-manifest.xml")`)
        and mark changed lines `✚`/`~` (greenfield → manifest only, no per-line marks); compress folds it to
        master downstream after the change ships. Then close with the integrity check per
        `AX_CLOSE_WITH_INTEGRITY_CHECK`: run `sdd-check --all specs/<scope>` (anchor
        balance + required sections + links) and resolve any finding. Then
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/review-lifecycle.directive.xml")` — internal critic →
        publish (MR) → external review → compress + merge on approval. Only after the spec merges to master,
        hand off to the `module` flow per `AX_HANDOFF_TO_MODULE_DECOMPOSITION`. Approval Check. STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>

  <ChatOutput>
    Service line — dim, internal, never narrated (per `AX_NO_PROCESS_NARRATION`):
    `🦾 DSC_R<N> · <scope> · <scope-type> · <mode> · conf=<LOW|MEDIUM|HIGH>`. Breadcrumb milestones
    (per `BREADCRUMB_FORMAT`): Intent · Requirements · Golden DX · Architecture · Rules · Spec.
    Disputes / dives open a nested frame on the main path per `AX_STACK_BASED_FLOW`; render the
    dive per `SIDE_DIVE_FORMAT` and return to the parent frame.

